{"raw": {"https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Consortium-Student-Wellness-and-Care-Coordinator.pdf": {"title": "Consortium Student Wellness and Care Coordinator", "description": "Consortium Student Wellness and Care Coordinator.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nTITLE: Consortium Student Wellness and Care Coordinator \nStudent-Facing Title:  Care Coach \n  REPORTS TO: Dean of Student Affairs \nDEPARTMENT: Academic Affairs \nSUPERVISES: Student peer ambassadors, as assigned \nSTATUS: Full-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Non-exempt, Grant-Funded \nSALARY RANGE:  $55,000-$60,000 \n   \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \n \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo; a metropolitan area known for \nits affordability, its four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d.   \n \nMISSION STATEMENT:  \n \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n \n \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need, \nand Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \n \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations \nfor our collective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on \ncompassion, trust, and authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and \nemployees who contribute to the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure \nthat all who join our inclusive community have what they need to realize their full \npotential. \n \n\n \n \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY: \n \nThe Consortium Student Wellness and Care Coordinator provides non-clinical care \ncoordination, student outreach, resource navigation, wellness education, and referral \nfollow-up for students at Villa Maria College, Niagara University, and Trocaire College. The \nCoordinator serves as a visible and accessible point of connection, helping students \nlocate and engage with on-campus, community-based, and virtual mental health and \nwellness resources. \nUsing a coordinated-care approach modeled on the community health worker framework, \nthe Coordinator builds student self-advocacy, promotes wellness and belonging, trains \npeer ambassadors, and strengthens collaboration across the three institutions. The \nposition is based at Villa Maria College and maintains a rotating in-person and hybrid \npresence across the participating campuses. This is a non-clinical position and does not \nprovide psychotherapy, diagnose mental health conditions, or replace licensed counseling \nor emergency services. \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n \n\u2022 Provide non-clinical care coordination and individualized resource navigation for \nreferred and self-referred students. \n\u2022 Help students identify and access appropriate mental health, wellness, social service, \nacademic support, community, and telehealth resources. \n\u2022 Develop and maintain clear referral pathways and follow up with students to support \nsuccessful connections and continuity of care. \n\u2022 Maintain an accessible presence through campus office hours, classroom visits, \nstudent events, orientation activities, workshops, tabling, and virtual engagement. \n\u2022 Develop low-barrier outreach and programming that normalizes help-seeking, reduces \nstigma, and strengthens student belonging. \n\u2022 Provide workshops and coaching focused on self-advocacy, resource literacy, stress \nmanagement, coping skills, and wellness. \n\u2022 Recruit, train, and coordinate student peer ambassadors or peer wellness coaches in \ncollaboration with student-life personnel. \n\u2022 Collaborate with counseling and wellness personnel, student affairs, academic affairs, \nstudent life, accessibility services, faculty, staff, and other student-support offices. \n\u2022 Partner with faculty and staff to support early identification and appropriate referral of \nstudents who may need assistance. \n\u2022 Coordinate wellness programming across participating institutions while respecting \neach campus\u2019s identity, systems, and resources. \n\u2022 Maintain accurate and confidential documentation of student contacts, referrals, \nfollow-up activities, workshops, events, and outreach. \n\u2022 Track engagement, referral completion, program participation, and feedback; prepare \nperiodic program summaries and recommendations. \n\u2022 Collaborate with institutional leaders and grant personnel to support external funding \nand continued development of the consortium model. \n\u2022 Follow applicable crisis-response, escalation, privacy, and mandated-reporting \nprotocols. \n \n \nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 Master\u2019s degree in social work, counseling, public health, higher education, student \naffairs, or a related field. \n\u2022 Experience working in higher education or with college-aged, commuter, adult, first-\ngeneration, or historically underserved students. \n\u2022 Experience with a community health worker, coordinated-care, case management, or \nstudent-success coaching model. \n\u2022 Experience developing wellness, prevention, self-advocacy, or student-belonging \nprogramming. \n\u2022 Experience recruiting, training, or coordinating peer educators, mentors, or student \nambassadors. \n\u2022 Knowledge of mental health, wellness, basic needs, and social-service resources in \nWestern New York. \n\u2022 Experience collecting program data, tracking referrals, assessing outcomes, or \nsupporting grant-funded initiatives. \n\u2022 Familiarity with trauma-informed, culturally responsive, and evidence-informed \nstudent- \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \n \nThe position requires regular travel among Villa Maria College, Niagara University, and \nTrocaire College and includes both in-person and virtual student engagement. The \nemployee will regularly interact with students experiencing stress or seeking mental \nhealth, wellness, or social-service resources. The position requires discretion, sound \njudgment, professional boundaries, and adherence to institutional privacy and response \nprotocols. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be required. If use of a vehicle is \nrequired for college purposes, a valid New York State driver\u2019s license check may be \nrequired. \n \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and employs individuals regardless of \ngender, race, color, religion, national origin, ancestry, age, marital status, sexual orientation, \npregnancy, physical or mental disability, citizenship, veteran status, gender expression and/or \nidentity, or any other class protected by federal, state, or local laws in admissions, employment, \nor any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. Should you \nrequire accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the counsel of the \nDirector of Human Resources for assistance. \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/VMC-Athletics-Mens-Basketball-Assistant-Coach-PT-Job-Description-002-1.pdf": {"title": "Assistant Coach \u2013 Men\u2019s Basketball", "description": "Assistant Coach \u2013 Men\u2019s Basketball.  \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \n \nTITLE:   Part-Time Assistant Coach \u2013 Men\u2019s Basketball \nDEPARTMENT:  Athletics  \nREPORTS TO:  Head Coach and Athletic Director \nSUPERVISES: None \nSTATUS :  Part-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt, Contract   \nDATE UPDATED: September 3, 2026 \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo, a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, and \nauthenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute to \nthe richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n\u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY:   \nThe Assistant Coach position manages assigned aspects of the men\u2019s basketball program as overseen by \nthe Head Coach and/or Director of Athletics. In communication with the Head Coach, the Assistant \nCoach works independently to manage targeted practice and game preparation and logistics, season \nadministration, player development, athletic training, travel, and recruitment of new players for the \nprogram. Recruitment of players is a key aspect of this position. \n  \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES \nThe candidate must demonstrate a strong professional work ethic and unwavering commitment to the \nacademic success of students and mission of the college. Must be goal oriented, able to motivate teams \nand collaboration among student team members.  \n \n \n \n \n2 \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred; Associate\u2019s degree required.   \n\u2022 Two years of coaching experience is encouraged, with preference given to collegiate level \nexperience.  \n\u2022 Must be able to recruit student-athletes to meet enrollment goals.   \n\u2022 Candidates should have strong interpersonal and leadership skills and ability to recruit quality \nstudent-athletes. \n\u2022 Must be able to work in the evenings and on weekends throughout the season and off-season. \n\u2022 Must have a current/valid NYS driver's license and an acceptable driving record. \n \nESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: \n\u2022 General office environment requires the employee to be flexible throughout the day to include \nhours standing, sitting, and walking (including up and down stairs), lifting and moving up to 25-\npound boxes. Typical duties include sitting at a desk, manual dexterity using hands and fingers \nto use computers and various office equipment. Professional communication is required for \nfrequent contact with others (in person or over phone/email), dealing with interruptions, and \nvarious noise levels. \n\u2022 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the \nessential functions. \n \nBENEFITS OF WORKING AT VILLA: \n\u2022 Retirement plan offering generous employer match \n\u2022 Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance plans with spouse, domestic partner and dependent \ncoverage available. \n\u2022 Vacation and sick time package based on length of tenure \n\u2022 Summer schedule hours (varies based on job duties) \n\u2022 13 paid holidays, plus a full week for Winter Break \n\u2022 Tuition exchange and tuition waiver benefits \n\u2022 An overall outstanding work culture with an opportunity to make a positive impact on students \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/VMC-Athletics-Womens-Basketball-Assistant-Coach-PT-Job-Description-003.pdf": {"title": "Assistant Coach \u2013 Women\u2019s Basketball", "description": "Assistant Coach \u2013 Women\u2019s Basketball.  \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \n \nTITLE:   Part-Time Assistant Coach \u2013 Women\u2019s Basketball \nDEPARTMENT:  Athletics  \nREPORTS TO:  Head Coach and Athletic Director \nSUPERVISES: None   \nSTATUS: Part-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt, Contract  \nSALARY RANGE:  $5,500.00-$6,500.00  \nDATE UPDATED: September 28, 2026 \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo, a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, and \nauthenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute to \nthe richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n\u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY:   \nThe Assistant Coach position manages assigned aspects of the women\u2019s basketball program as overseen \nby the Head Coach and/or Director of Athletics. In communication with the Head Coach, the Assistant \nCoach works independently to manage targeted practice and game preparation and logistics, season \nadministration, player development, athletic training, travel, and recruitment of new players for the \nprogram. Recruitment of players is a key aspect of this position. \n  \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nThe candidate must demonstrate a strong professional work ethic and unwavering commitment to the \nacademic success of students and mission of the college. Must be goal oriented, able to motivate teams \nand collaboration among student team members.  \n \n \n \n2 \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred; Associate\u2019s degree required.   \n\u2022 Two years of coaching experience is encouraged, with preference given to collegiate level \nexperience.  \n\u2022 Must be able to recruit student-athletes to meet enrollment goals.   \n\u2022 Candidates should have strong interpersonal and leadership skills and ability to recruit quality \nstudent-athletes. \n\u2022 Must be able to work in the evenings and on weekends throughout the season and off-season. \n\u2022 Must have a current/valid NYS driver's license and an acceptable driving record. \n \nESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: \n\u2022 General office environment requires the employee to be flexible throughout the day to include \nhours standing, sitting, and walking (including up and down stairs), lifting and moving up to 25-\npound boxes. Typical duties include sitting at a desk, manual dexterity using hands and fingers \nto use computers and various office equipment. Professional communication is required for \nfrequent contact with others (in person or over phone/email), dealing with interruptions, and \nvarious noise levels. \n\u2022 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the \nessential functions. \n \nBENEFITS OF WORKING AT VILLA: \n\u2022 Retirement plan offering generous employer match \n\u2022 Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance plans with spouse, domestic partner and dependent \ncoverage available. \n\u2022 Vacation and sick time package based on length of tenure \n\u2022 Summer schedule hours (varies based on job duties) \n\u2022 13 paid holidays, plus a full week for Winter Break \n\u2022 Tuition exchange and tuition waiver benefits \n\u2022 An overall outstanding work culture with an opportunity to make a positive impact on students \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/WFF-Second-Assistant-Coach.pdf": {"title": "Second Assistant Coach \u2013 Women\u2019s Flag Football", "description": "Second Assistant Coach \u2013 Women\u2019s Flag Football.  \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \n \nTITLE:   Second Assistant Coach  \u2013 Women\u2019s Flag Football \nDEPARTMENT:  Athletics  \nREPORTS TO:  Head Coach  \nSUPERVISES: None \nSTATUS :  Part-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt, Contract   \nDATE UPDATED: September, 2026 \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo, a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, and \nauthenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute to \nthe richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n\u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY:   \nThe Assistant Coach position manages assigned aspects of the women\u2019s flag football program as \noverseen by the Head Coach, and is the head coach of the second/JV team. In communication with the \nHead Coach, the Assistant Coach works independently to manage targeted practice and game \npreparation and logistics, season administration, player development, athletic training, travel, and \nrecruitment of new players for the program. Recruitment of players is a key aspect of this position. \n  \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nThe candidate must demonstrate a strong professional work ethic and unwavering commitment to the \nacademic success of students and mission of the college. Must be goal oriented, able to motivate teams \nand collaboration among student team members.  \n \n \n \n \n2 \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 Bachelor\u2019s degree preferred; Associate\u2019s degree required.   \n\u2022 Two years of coaching experience is encouraged, with preference given to collegiate level \nexperience.  \n\u2022 Must be able to recruit student-athletes to meet enrollment goals.   \n\u2022 Candidates should have strong interpersonal and leadership skills and ability to recruit quality \nstudent-athletes. \n\u2022 Must be able to work in the evenings and on weekends throughout the season and off-season. \n\u2022 Must have a current/valid NYS driver's license and an acceptable driving record. \n \nESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS: \n\u2022 General office environment requires the employee to be flexible throughout the day to include \nhours standing, sitting, and walking (including up and down stairs), lifting and moving up to 25-\npound boxes. Typical duties include sitting at a desk, manual dexterity using hands and fingers \nto use computers and various office equipment. Professional communication is required for \nfrequent contact with others (in person or over phone/email), dealing with interruptions, and \nvarious noise levels. \n\u2022 Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable individuals with disabilities to perform the \nessential functions. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Animation-Adjunct-092223.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Animation Adjunct", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Animation Adjunct.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nANIMATION \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nTeach advanced 3D animation techniques in Autodesk Maya with a focus on the introduction to \ncharacter rigging and character animation. Handle all aspects of instructing undergraduate courses \nin the BFA in Animation program, including organizing lectures/demonstrations, generating and \ndistributing assignments, assisting students with technical and creative questions related to \nassignments, and grading. \n \n \nQUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 MFA in Animation is preferred; alternative degrees will be considered. \n\u2022 Preference given to candidates with teaching experience. \n\u2022 Animation or Game Design industry experience a plus. \n\u2022 Proficiency in 3D Animation software including Autodesk Maya is required. \n\u2022 Knowledge of 2D compositing software including Adobe After Effects is \nrequired. \n\u2022 Outstanding communication skills. \n\u2022 Excellent managerial and classroom management skills. \n \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, online portfolio or \ndemo reel, statement of teaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Bass-Instructor-092323.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Bass Instructor", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Bass Instructor.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nMUSIC DEPARTMENT \nBASS INSTRUCTOR \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY: \nThe position provides instruction in electric and stand-up bass. The College offers a B.A. in \nMusic and a B.S. in Music Industry, as well a minor in Jazz, a minor in Performance, and a \ntrack in Advanced Production. Students learn traditional theory and have the opportunity to \nstudy classical genres. With ensembles in Jazz, Gospel, Hip-Hop, and Rock, among others, \nthere is a strong emphasis on the popular music industry. \n \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nTeach one-on-one lessons to Villa Maria bass students. Lesso        our with the \npossibility of a full hour lesson depending on student program. \n \n \nQUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 A master\u2019s degree in Music is preferred but candidates with a four-year degree are \nencouraged to apply. \n\u2022 Industry experience required. \n\u2022 Teaching experience preferred. \n\u2022 Preference will be given to candidates with teaching experience at the college level. \n \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, online portfolio or \ndemo reel, statement of teaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $320 per Student per semester \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Anatomy-Bio-Physics-Adjunct-092223.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Biology, Anatomy, and Physics", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Biology, Anatomy, and Physics.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nANATOMY, BIOLOGY, PHYSICS \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nThe faculty member will handle all aspects of foundational science courses including organizing \nlectures, demonstrations, generating and distributing assignments, assisting students with \ntechnical and creative questions related to \nassignments and grading. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \nMinimum of a Master\u2019s Degree in the field or related professional degree. \nPreference will be given to candidates with teaching experience at the college level. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, statement of \nteaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Business-Administration-Job-Description-PT-faculty.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Business Administration", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Business Administration.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nTITLE: Business Administration Part-Time Faculty Member \n  REPORTS TO: Program Chair \nDEPARTMENT: Academic Affairs \nSTATUS: Part-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt \n  SALARY RANGE:      $700 per credit hour \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo; a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, its four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d.   \n \nMISSION STATEMENT:  \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations \nfor our collective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on \ncompassion, trust, and authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and \nemployees who contribute to the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure \nthat all who join our inclusive community have what they need to realize their full \npotential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY: \nThe ideal candidate will be responsible for teaching Business Administration courses.  \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n \n\u2022 Teach foundational undergraduate course(s) such as: ECO 220 \u2013 Personal \nFinancial Planning \n\u2022 Provide student-centered instruction in all courses; \n\u2022 Provide direction and climate for effective learning; \n\n\u2022 Design means of evaluating and improving the teaching/learning \nprocess in the classroom; \n\u2022 Review and develop curricula; \n\u2022 Submit attendance, grades, and required reports to appropriate offices; \n\u2022 Assist the Department Chairperson in assessing the effectiveness of the \nprogram; \n\u2022 Support the mission and objectives of the College. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n \n\u2022 Master\u2019s degree in field or other closely related field. \n\u2022 Preference given to candidates with teaching experience. \n\u2022 Outstanding communication skills. \n\u2022 Excellent managerial and classroom management skills.  \n\u2022 Experience working in a small, private, liberal arts institution with traditional and non-\ntraditional students is preferred. \n\u2022 Candidates with a Bachelor\u2019s degree in business or a related field will be considered if \nthey possess substantial professional experience in personal finance or hold additional \nrelevant professional credentials. Preference will be given to applicants with college-\nlevel teaching experience. \n \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nGeneral work environment requires the employee to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom/office space. This position requires fully \nfunctional vision and auditory abilities. This position may include hours standing and walking, \nincluding up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Occasional evening and \nweekend hours may be needed to perform work associated with this position. If the position \nrequires use of vehicle for College purposes, a valid New York State driver\u2019s license check may \nbe required for occasional off- campus assistance and support. \n \nBENEFITS OF WORKING AT VILLA: \n-Retirement plan offering generous employer match \n-Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance plans with spouse, domestic partner and dependent \ncoverage available. \n-Vacation and sick time package based on length of tenure \n-Summer schedule hours (varies based on job duties) \n-13 paid holidays, plus a full week for Winter Break \n-Tuition exchange and tuition waiver benefits \n-An overall outstanding work culture with an opportunity to make a positive impact on students \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/Criminal-Justice-Job-Description.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Criminal Justice", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Criminal Justice. JOB DESCRIPTION \nTITLE:     Criminal Justice Adjunct Faculty \nDEPARTMENT:   Criminal Justice \nREPORTS TO:   Chair, Criminal Justice Dept. \nSUPERVISES:   None \nSTATUS:     Part-time, Contract \nCLASSIFICATION:   Exempt \n \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides \nstudents a rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs \nwith a broad core curriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize \ntheir intellectual, creative, professional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming \nCatholic tradition and a dynamic Franciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual \nattention and fosters compassion, justice, peace, respect for human dignity and a \ncommitment to service. \u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace. \u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY: Responsible for teaching undergraduate courses in the criminal \njustice or crime scene investigation curriculum. This includes handling all aspects of the \ncourses including organizing lectures, demonstrations, generating and distributing \nassignments, assisting students with questions related to assignments and grading.  \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: Minimum of a bachelor\u2019s degree in criminal justice or a \nrelated \ufb01eld. Master\u2019s degree preferred. Preference will be given to candidates with \nteaching experience. Provide student-centered instruction in all courses; Provide direction \nand climate for effective learning; Submit attendance, grades, and required reports to \nappropriate offices; Assist the Department Chairperson in assessing the effectiveness of \nthe program; Support the mission and objectives of the College \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: Professional office/classroom environment requires employee to \nbe \ufb02exible, consistently use manual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the \nclassroom, lab, or office. This position requires fully functional vision and auditory abilities. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work \nbeing performed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties \nand responsibilities.  \n \nVilla Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change responsibilities to \nmeet business and organizational needs as necessary. Villa Maria College is an equal \nopportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, race, religion, creed, \ncolor, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, marital status, \nphysical or mental disability, or any other protected classi\ufb01cations in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek \nthe counsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.  \n \n \n \n \n_________________________________________________  _________________________  \nEmployee Signature       Date "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/01/Job-Description-DFM-Adjunct.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Digital Filmmaking Adjunct", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Digital Filmmaking Adjunct.  \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \n \nTITLE:  Digital Filmmaking Faculty Member  \nDEPARTMENT:  Art Department  \nREPORTS TO:  Dean of Faculty  \nSUPERVISES: None  \nSTATUS:  Part-Time, Contract \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt \n \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY:  \nResponsible for teaching the basic tools and techniques for Digital Filmmaking, which could \ninclude Film Theory and Technique, Production Design, Film Editing and Lighting, Sound \nDesign, Production Management, Screenwriting and Directing.  \n \n \nQUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022   Master's degree (MFA or MA) in Film, Digital Media, Communications or related field. \n\u2022   College-level teaching experience preferred. \n\u2022   Strong portfolio in digital filmmaking or related field. \n\u2022   Proficiency with Adobe Production Premium, Microsoft Office Suite, Avid M Box, and      \n  Final Cut Pro. \n\u2022   Should be familiar with all aspects of camera operations and post-production    \n  processes. \n \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT:  \nGeneral classroom environment requires employees to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom. This position requires fully functional vision \nand auditory abilities. This position may include hours standing and walking, including up and \ndown stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Occasional evening and weekend hours may be \nneeded to perform work associated with this position. If the position requires use of vehicle for \nCollege purposes, a valid New York State driver\u2019s license check may be required for occasional \noff- campus assistance and support. \n \n \n\n \n \n \n2 \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \n \n____________________________________  ________________________ \nEmployee Signature      Date \n   \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/English-Adjunct-092323.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 English", "description": "Faculty \u2013 English.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nENGLISH \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY \nPart-time faculty members are primarily expected to teach first-year writing courses. Additional \nwriting and literature courses may be available and will be assigned by area of expertise. The \nteaching load is a minimum of 3 credit hour equivalencies per semester. Part-time faculty are \nexpected to provide student centered instruction in all courses, foster a climate of effective \nlearning,and participate in the planning and implementation of programs. \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n\u2022 Teach a minimum of 3 credit hour equivalences per year. \n\u2022 Provide student-centered instruction in all courses. \n\u2022 Foster a climate of effective learning. \n\u2022 Design means of evaluating and improving the teaching/learning process in the \nclassroom. \n\u2022 Pursue professional development and growth. \n\u2022 Review and develop curricula. \n\u2022 Participate in program assessment activities. \n\u2022 Participate in program and College accreditation activities. \n\u2022 Submit required reports to appropriate offices. \n\u2022 Attend scheduled program meetings and maintain regular office hours. \n\u2022 Develop plans for the use of equipment, instructional aids, and supplies. \n \n\u2022 Support the mission and objectives of the College. \n\u2022 Assume other work-related responsibilities as assigned by the Department Chair, the Vice \nPresident for Academic Affairs, or the President or his/her designee as needed to meet \nthe needs of the College mission. \n \nMINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS \nM.A. in English or closely related field, with a strong record of teaching first-year composition \nand demonstrated success in teaching diverse student populations. \n \nDESIRED QUALIFICATIONS \nPh.D. in English or closely related field. An experienced teacher with a portfolio that includes \nfirst year composition. Experience in teaching professional and technical writing is desired. \nInterest in multiple classroom literacies, learning differences, or writing program administration \nis welcome. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, statement of \nteaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \n \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Fine-Arts-Adjunct-092223-1.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Fine Arts", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Fine Arts.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nFINE ARTS INSTRUCTOR \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY \nThe faculty member will handle all aspects of instructing undergraduate course(s) such as 2D \nDesign, Drawing, and History of Art within the Fine Arts program including organizing lectures, \ndemonstrations, generating and distributing assignments, assisting students with \ntechnical and creative questions related to assignments and grading. \n \nQUALIFICATIONS \n\u2022 Master\u2019s degree in fine arts or related field required. \n\u2022 Preference will be given to candidates with experience teaching art at the college level. \n\u2022 Experience teaching foundation courses (2D design, drawing and history of art). \n\u2022 Outstanding communication skills. Must be able to interact and communicate \neffectively with students. \n\u2022 Ability to teach both lecture and studio courses is required. \n\u2022 Strong commitment to learn and be self-motivated. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \n \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: \n\u2022 Cover letter \n\u2022 Curriculum vitae and/or resume \n\u2022 5-7 samples of scholarly or creative work and student creative work \n\u2022 Link to an online portfolio \n\u2022 Statement of teaching philosophy \n\u2022  \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Graphic-Design-Adjunct-092223.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Graphic Design Instructor", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Graphic Design Instructor.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nGRAPHIC DESIGN  \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nTeach a freshman-level Graphic Design course \n. \n \nQUALIFICATIONS: \nMaster's degree (MFA or MA) in graphic design or closely related field preferred. \n\u2022 Strong portfolio in graphic design or related field. \n\u2022 In-depth knowledge of the fundamental and advanced principles and theories of visual \ncommunication and graphic design. \n\u2022 Proficiency in Macintosh operating system and Adobe Creative Cloud Software. \n\u2022 Excellent oral and written communication skills, leadership qualities with passion for \nteaching. \n\u2022 Interpersonal skills with the ability to effectively communicate with students. \n\u2022 College-level teaching experience in graphic design preferred. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, statement of \nteaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Interior-Design-Job-Description-PT-faculty-051925.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Interior Design", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Interior Design.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nTITLE: Part-Time Faculty Member for Portfolio Design \n  REPORTS TO: Program Chair \nDEPARTMENT: Academic Affairs \nSTATUS: Part-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt \n  SALARY:      $700 per credit hour  \n \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo; a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, its four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d.   \n \nMISSION STATEMENT:  \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, and \nauthenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute to \nthe richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY:  \nThe Interior Design program at Villa Maria College is looking for part-time faculty to teach one or \nmore of the following courses: \n\u2022 CAD 2 \n\u2022 Thesis Pre-Design \n\u2022 Portfolio Design \nCourse descriptions can be found in Villa Maria College\u2019s course catalog on our Registrar\u2019s site \nat https://www.villa.edu/academics/registrar/ under Academic Catalog. \n  \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n\n \n\u2022 Provide student-centered instruction in all courses; \n\u2022 Provide direction and climate for effective learning; \n\u2022 Design means of evaluating and improving the teaching/learning process in \nthe classroom; \n\u2022 Review and develop curricula; \n\u2022 Submit attendance, grades, and required reports to appropriate offices; \n\u2022 Assist the Department Chairperson in assessing the effectiveness of the program; \n\u2022 Support the mission and objectives of the College. \n \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n \n\u2022 Master\u2019s Degree Preferred, Bachelor\u2019s degree required. \n\u2022 Proficiency in Revit and/or AutoCAD in a professional and/or academic capacity is \ndesired. \n\u2022 Experience with graphic design and digital presentations desired Preference given to \ncandidates with teaching experience. \n\u2022 Outstanding communication skills. \n\u2022 Excellent managerial and classroom management skills.  \n\u2022 Experience working in a small, private, liberal arts institution with traditional and non- \ntraditional aged students is preferred. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nGeneral work environment requires the employee to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom/office space. This position requires fully \nfunctional vision and auditory abilities. This position may include hours standing and walking, \nincluding up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Occasional evening and \nweekend hours may be needed to perform work associated with this position. If the position \nrequires use of vehicle for College purposes, a valid New York State driver\u2019s license check may \nbe required for occasional off- campus assistance and support. \n \nBENEFITS OF WORKING AT VILLA: \n-Retirement plan offering generous employer match \n-Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance plans with spouse, domestic partner and dependent \ncoverage available. \n-Vacation and sick time package based on length of tenure \n-Summer schedule hours (varies based on job duties) \n-13 paid holidays, plus a full week for Winter Break \n-Tuition exchange and tuition waiver benefits \n-An overall outstanding work culture with an opportunity to make a positive impact on students \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. \n \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Math-Adjunct-092223.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Mathematics", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Mathematics.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nMATHEMATICS \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nTeach foundational undergraduate course(s) such as: MAT 110, Introduction to College \nMathematics; MAT 111, College Algebra. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \nMinimum of Master\u2019s Degree in math or related field required. \nPreference will be given to candidates with teaching experience at the college level. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, statement of \nteaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/PHO-PT-Faculty.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Photography", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Photography.  \n \nPHOTOGRAPHY PROGRAM \nPART-TIME INSTRUCTOR \nTITLE: Part-Time Instructor, Photography Program \nREPORTS TO: Program Chair \nDEPARTMENT: Academic Affairs \nSTATUS: Part-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt \nSALARY:  $700 per credit hour (studio courses are 4 CHE\u2019s so a semester long \ncourse is $2800 total) \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY \nThe Photography Program at Villa Maria College is currently accepting applications for a  \npart-time instructor for the upcoming Spring 2027 semester. The ideal candidate will be responsible \nfor teaching PHO 201 Photo Imaging and Design and/or PHO 301 Advanced Digital Imaging. \nProficient in digital photography and Adobe Software including Photoshop, Bridge, Lightroom. Video \nediting software (PHO 301 only) such as Photoshop, Premiere or iMovie. As well as a knowledge of \nphotography history. The spring semester begins January 19, 2027, and goes to May 6, 2027. \n \nCourses will run as follows:  \nPHO 201B Photo Imaging and Design T/Th 3:10-5:40 (freshman) \nPHO 301A Advanced Digital Imaging M/W 3:10-5:40 (juniors and seniors) \n \nCourse descriptions: \nPHO 201 \u2013 Photo Imaging and Design \nAn introduction to digital manipulation of photography combined with graphics using the latest \nsoftware and/or industry software standards as applied to fine art and commercial works. For \nprogram major or minor requirements, a grade of C or above is required for successful completion. \nA studio course. 3 credits \n \nPHO 301 \u2013 Advanced Digital Imaging \nAdvanced Digital Imaging will explore still and time-based imagery. A continuation of PHO 201 \nPhoto Imaging and Design, Advanced Digital Imaging explores the creation and presentation of \ndigital art. Working within historical and contemporary art contexts, a variety of image, motion, and \nsound editing and presentation applications will be covered within the course. For program major or \nminor requirements, a grade of C or above is required for successful completion. Prerequisite: \nGrade of C or above in PHO 201. A studio course. 3 credits \n \nQUALIFICATIONS  \n\u2022 Master's degree (MFA or MA) in photography or closely related field or currently pursuing \nthis degree required.  \n\u2022 2 years of college-level teaching experience in photography preferred with strong portfolio in \nphotography or related field. \n\u2022 Proficiency in Macintosh operating system and Adobe Software. \n\u2022 Excellent oral and written communication skills, leadership qualities with passion for \nteaching. \n\n\u2022 Interpersonal skills with the ability to effectively communicate with students. \n \nESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS:  \nGeneral environment requires employee to be flexible. This work may include hours standing and \nwalking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Evening and weekend \nhours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work associated with this position. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. Villa Maria College is an \nequal Opportunity Employer. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: \n\u2022 Cover letter \n\u2022 Curriculum vitae and/or resume \n\u2022 Statement of teaching philosophy \n\u2022 Three references \n \nTO APPLY: Please complete the online job application at Jobs.villa.edu. When you have completed \nthe on-line application and have uploaded the requested materials, your information will be \nforwarded to the Search Committee for review. The Search Committee will carefully review each \nresume, and the strongest, most qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of age, \nrace, religion or creed, color, sex, national or ethnic origin, marital status, or physical or mental \ndisability in admissions, employment, or in any other aspect regarding the conduct of College \nprograms and activities. \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT:  \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, and \nauthenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute to the \nrichness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive community \nhave what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo; a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, its four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, and \nauthenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute to \nthe richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n\u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n \n\u2022 Provide student-centered instruction in all courses; \n\u2022 Provide direction and climate for effective learning; \n\u2022 Design means of evaluating and improving the teaching/learning process in \nthe classroom; \n\u2022 Review and develop curricula; \n\u2022 Submit attendance, grades, and required reports to appropriate offices; \n\u2022 Assist the Department Chairperson in assessing the effectiveness of the program; \n\u2022 Support the mission and objectives of the College. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n \n\u2022 Master\u2019s degree in field other closely related field. \n\u2022 Preference given to candidates with teaching experience. \n\u2022 Outstanding communication skills. \n\u2022 Excellent managerial and classroom management skills. \n\u2022 Experience working in a small, private, liberal arts institution with traditional and non-\ntraditional aged students is preferred. \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nGeneral work environment requires the employee to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom/office space. This position requires fully \nfunctional vision and auditory abilities. This position may include hours standing and walking, \nincluding up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Occasional evening and \nweekend hours may be needed to perform work associated with this position. If the position \nrequires use of vehicle for College purposes, a valid New York State driver\u2019s license check may \nbe required for occasional off- campus assistance and support. \nBENEFITS OF WORKING AT VILLA: \n-Retirement plan offering generous employer match \n-Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance plans with spouse, domestic partner and dependent \ncoverage available. \n-Vacation and sick time package based on length of tenure \n-Summer schedule hours (varies based on job duties) \n-13 paid holidays, plus a full week for Winter Break \n-Tuition exchange and tuition waiver benefits \n-An overall outstanding work culture with an opportunity to make a positive impact on students \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Chemistry-Adjunct-092323.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Physics and Chemistry", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Physics and Chemistry.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nCHEMISTRY \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nTeach foundational undergraduate course(s) such as: CHE 101, General Chemistry I or CHE \n102, General Chemistry II. \n \nQUALIFICATIONS: \nMinimum of a Master\u2019s Degree in Chemistry or related discipline. \nPreference will be given to candidates with teaching experience at the college level. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \n \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, statement of \nteaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/Social-Sciences-Adjunct-092223.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Social Sciences Adjunct", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Social Sciences Adjunct.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nSOCIAL SCIENCES \nADJUNCT FACULTY MEMBER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity \nwith the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \nThe faculty member will teach foundational undergraduate course(s) such as Principles of \nSociology, Contemporary Social Problems, Global Citizenship, or Cultural Anthropology. \nThis includes handling all aspects of the courses including organizing lectures, demonstrations, \ngenerating and distributing assignments, assisting students with questions related to \nassignments and grading. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \nMinimum of Master\u2019s degree with a specialization in anthropology, sociology, or a related field. \nPhD students who have advanced to candidacy are encouraged to apply.  Preference will be \ngiven to candidates with teaching experience at the college level. \n. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \n \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS \nApplicants should include: cover letter, curriculum vitae or resume, statement of \nteaching philosophy and three references. \n \nAPPLICATION PROCESS \nPlease submit application materials to jobs.villa.edu . When you have completed the \nonline application process your information will be forwarded to the search committee \nfor review. The search committee will carefully review each resume and the strongest, \nmost qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $700 per Credit Hour Equivalent (CHE) \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/Sport-Management-Job-Description-PT-faculty.pdf": {"title": "Faculty \u2013 Sport Management", "description": "Faculty \u2013 Sport Management.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nTITLE: Sport Management Part-Time Faculty Member \n  REPORTS TO: Program Chair \nDEPARTMENT: Academic Affairs \nSTATUS: Full-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt \n  SALARY RANGE:      $700 per credit hour \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo; a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, its four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d.   \n \nMISSION STATEMENT:  \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations \nfor our collective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on \ncompassion, trust, and authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and \nemployees who contribute to the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure \nthat all who join our inclusive community have what they need to realize their full \npotential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY: \nThe ideal candidate will be responsible for teaching Sport Management courses.  \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n \n\u2022 Provide student-centered instruction in all courses; \n\u2022 Provide direction and climate for effective learning; \n\u2022 Design means of evaluating and improving the teaching/learning \nprocess in the classroom; \n\n\u2022 Review and develop curricula; \n\u2022 Submit attendance, grades, and required reports to appropriate offices; \n\u2022 Assist the Department Chairperson in assessing the effectiveness of the \nprogram; \n\u2022 Support the mission and objectives of the College. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n \n\u2022 Master\u2019s degree in field or other closely related field. \n\u2022 Preference given to candidates with teaching experience. \n\u2022 Outstanding communication skills. \n\u2022 Excellent managerial and classroom management skills.  \n\u2022 Experience working in a small, private, liberal arts institution with traditional and non-\ntraditional students is preferred. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nGeneral work environment requires the employee to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom/office space. This position requires fully \nfunctional vision and auditory abilities. This position may include hours standing and walking, \nincluding up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Occasional evening and \nweekend hours may be needed to perform work associated with this position. If the position \nrequires use of vehicle for College purposes, a valid New York State driver\u2019s license check may \nbe required for occasional off- campus assistance and support. \n \nBENEFITS OF WORKING AT VILLA: \n-Retirement plan offering generous employer match \n-Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance plans with spouse, domestic partner and dependent \ncoverage available. \n-Vacation and sick time package based on length of tenure \n-Summer schedule hours (varies based on job duties) \n-13 paid holidays, plus a full week for Winter Break \n-Tuition exchange and tuition waiver benefits \n-An overall outstanding work culture with an opportunity to make a positive impact on students \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Professional-Tutor-2024.pdf": {"title": "Professional Tutor", "description": "Professional Tutor. 240 Pine Ridge Road, Buffalo, NY 14225     PHONE   716.896.0700  FAX   716.896.0705  \nPROFESSIONAL TUTOR  \nPART TIME STAFF POSITION \nAbout Us: Villa Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier \nstudent-centered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally \ndiverse population that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity.  \nMission Statement:  \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students a \nrigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \nVilla Maria College Core Values:  \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, \nSolidarity with the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \nPOSITION SUMMARY:   \nUnder the daily direction of the Student Success Center staff, the Professional Tutor will,\nprovide individual and small group tutoring to students in the Student Success Center for the \nCollege. Assist students in improving academic achievement by meeting with them on a \nregular basis to clarify learning problems and work on study skills. Other assistance might \ninclude: reviewing class material, discussing the text, helping students with time management, \nassisting students with the writing process, or working on solutions to problems. \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n\uf0b7 Assist students academically in whichever subjects that you have expertise;\n\uf0b7 Develop education resources relevant to your subject area;\n\uf0b7 Facilitate, and track tutorial sessions;\n\uf0b7 Greet and interact with students professionally and enthusiastically;\n\uf0b7 Maintain communications with the Coordinators of the Student Success Center;\n\uf0b7 Encourage students and help them develop academic confidence;\n\uf0b7 Develop study skills specifically designed for the students' needs;\n\uf0b7 Evaluate students' progress in order to see where improvements can be made;\n\uf0b7 Take on additional responsibilities as assigned by the Coordinators of the Student\nSuccess Center;\n\uf0b7 Discuss daily concerns with the Coordinators of the Student Success Center;\n\uf0b7 Support the philosophy and objectives of the College;\n\uf0b7 Other duties as assigned to meet the mission of the College.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS: \n\uf0b7 Bachelor\u2019s Degree (minimum qualification);\n\uf0b7 Master\u2019s Degree or working toward Master\u2019s degree (preferred qualification);\n\uf0b7 Previous experience working with students;\n\uf0b7 Cumulative GPA of 3.0 and excelling grades in subjects of expertise;\n\uf0b7 Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Power point) knowledge necessary;\n\uf0b7 Knowledge of industry software to cover disciplines taught at VMC when applicable;\n\uf0b7 Excellent communication and relationship building skills.\nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary.  \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nGeneral classroom environment requires employees to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom/office/lab. This work may include hours \nstanding and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Evening \nand weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work associated with this position. \nAPPLICATION MATERIALS: \nApplicants should include 1) cover letter and 2) resume/curriculum vitae\nTo be considered, please submit your resume and complete the online job application at \njobs.villa.edu. When you have completed the on-line application process your information will \nbe forwarded to the Search Committee for review. The Search Committee will carefully review \neach resume and the strongest, most qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview.  \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion or creed, color, sex, national or ethnic origin, marital status, physical or \nmental disability, or any other protected category by Federal/State guidelines in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT:\nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our\ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust,\nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who \ncontribute to the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our \ninclusive community have what they need to realize their full potential."}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/JD-general-PT-faculty-002.pdf": {"title": "Part-Time Faculty Member \u2013 Pool Posting: Candidates will be contacted when an opening in the appropriate area occurs", "description": "Part-Time Faculty Member \u2013 Pool Posting: Candidates will be contacted when an opening in the appropriate area occurs.  \n \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nTITLE: Part-Time Faculty Member  \n  REPORTS TO: Program Chair \nDEPARTMENT: Academic Affairs \nSTATUS: Part-Time \nCLASSIFICATION: Exempt \n  SALARY:      $700 per credit hour  \n \nThis is a pool posting and candidates will be contacted when an opening in the appropriate area \noccurs. \n \nABOUT VILLA MARIA COLLEGE: \nVilla Maria is a private higher education institution offering a wide variety of academic programs. \nVilla is located in Cheektowaga, New York, bordering the City of Buffalo; a metropolitan area \nknown for its affordability, its four seasons, and for being the \u201cCity of Good Neighbors\u201d.   \n \nMISSION STATEMENT:  \nVilla Maria College is a Catholic, Franciscan college, founded by the Felician Sisters, that uses \ninnovative strategies to educate and empower a diverse student body to positively impact their \ncommunities. \n \nDiversity Equity, Inclusion & Belonging Statement: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, and \nauthenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute to \nthe richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \n \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with People in need.\u201d \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n \n\u2022 Provide student-centered instruction in all courses; \n\u2022 Provide direction and climate for effective learning; \n\u2022 Design means of evaluating and improving the teaching/learning process in \nthe classroom; \n\u2022 Review and develop curricula; \n\n\u2022 Submit attendance, grades, and required reports to appropriate offices; \n\u2022 Assist the Department Chairperson in assessing the effectiveness of the program; \n\u2022 Support the mission and objectives of the College. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n \n\u2022 Master\u2019s degree in field other closely related field. \n\u2022 Preference given to candidates with teaching experience. \n\u2022 Outstanding communication skills. \n\u2022 Excellent managerial and classroom management skills.  \n\u2022 Experience working in a small, private, liberal arts institution with traditional and non- \ntraditional aged students is preferred. \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nGeneral work environment requires the employee to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom/office space. This position requires fully \nfunctional vision and auditory abilities. This position may include hours standing and walking, \nincluding up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Occasional evening and \nweekend hours may be needed to perform work associated with this position. If the position \nrequires use of vehicle for College purposes, a valid New York State driver\u2019s license check may \nbe required for occasional off- campus assistance and support. \n \nBENEFITS OF WORKING AT VILLA: \n-Retirement plan offering generous employer match \n-Health, Dental, Vision, and Life Insurance plans with spouse, domestic partner and dependent \ncoverage available. \n-Vacation and sick time package based on length of tenure \n-Summer schedule hours (varies based on job duties) \n-13 paid holidays, plus a full week for Winter Break \n-Tuition exchange and tuition waiver benefits \n-An overall outstanding work culture with an opportunity to make a positive impact on students \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance. \n \n \n \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2023/09/orientation-leader-092223.pdf": {"title": "Student Worker \u2013 Orientation Leader", "description": "Student Worker \u2013 Orientation Leader.  \n \n \nJOB DESCRIPTION \n \nORIENTATION LEADER \n \nABOUT US:  \nVilla Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier student-\ncentered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally diverse \npopulation that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity. \n \nMISSION STATEMENT: \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students \na rigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \n \nOUR CORE VALUES: \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, Solidarity with \nthe Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \n \nPOSITION SUMMARY: \nNew Student Orientation serves to ease the transition of incoming students to college life and to \nmake them feel welcome in our Villa Maria College community. The Orientation Leader is a \nstudent leadership position that requires enthusiasm, dedication, and a positive view of Villa \nMaria College. All Orientation Leaders are expected to be team players who are interested in \nhelping new students succeed at Villa Maria. The Orientation Leader works directly with other \nOrientation Leaders, the Director of Student Life, Villa Maria College staff, and new students and \ntheir families.   \n \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n\u2022 Attend and actively participate in all required Orientation Leader training sessions. \n\u2022 Participate in and assist with all aspects of New Student Orientation. \n\u2022 Represent Villa Maria College and serve with a sense of professionalism and positivity. \n\u2022 Assist new students and their families in their transition to VMC by making them feel \nwelcome and at home. \n\u2022 Promote a heightened awareness and respect for diversity. \n\u2022 Increase students\u2019 awareness of the interconnectedness of the campus and \nBuffalo communities. \n\u2022 Serve as a knowledgeable resource of all aspects of VMC and New Student Orientation. \n\u2022 Serve as a positive role model by displaying appropriate and ethical behavior. \n \n\u2022 Other duties as assigned to meet the mission of the College. \n \nESSENTIAL QUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 Currently enrolled as a student at the institution with a 2.0 GPA or higher. \n\u2022 Ability to work with a diverse population \n\u2022 Ability to interact positively with peers, faculty, and staff \n\u2022 Demonstrated ability to serve as a positive role model \n\u2022 Good disciplinary/judicial standing \n\u2022 Ability to relate well with students, families, and administrators \n\u2022 Must be reliable and willing to help with all aspects of New Student Orientation \n\u2022 Must demonstrate enthusiasm for the Orientation Leader position \n\u2022 Must be available for all training dates and for all aspects of New Student Orientation \n \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nProfessional office/classroom environment requires employee to be flexible, consistently use \nmanual dexterity in reaching, writing, navigating around the classroom, lab, or office. This work \nmay include hours standing and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to \n25-pounds. Evening and weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work \nassociated with this position. Possible keyboarding movements will be necessary to perform \ncomputer work for this position. \n \nTo be considered, please complete the online job application at jobs.villa.edu. When you \nhave completed the on-line application process your information will be forwarded to the Search \nCommittee for review. The Search Committee will carefully review each application and the \nstrongest, most qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview. \n \nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary. \n \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion, creed, color, sex, sexual orientation or preference, national or ethnic origin, \nmarital status, physical or mental disability, or any other protected classifications in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nShould you require an accommodation, according to the guidelines of the ADA, please seek the \ncounsel of the Director of Human Resources for assistance.   \n \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT: \nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our \ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust, \nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who contribute \nto the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our inclusive \ncommunity have what they need to realize their full potential. \n \nSALARY RANGE:   $14.20 per hour \n "}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2024/08/Peer-Student-Tutor-2024.pdf": {"title": "Student Worker \u2013 Peer Student Tutor", "description": "Student Worker \u2013 Peer Student Tutor. 240 Pine Ridge Road, Buffalo, NY 14225     PHONE   716.896.0700  FAX   716.896.0705  \nPEER TUTOR  \nPART TIME STUDENT POSITION \nAbout Us: Villa Maria College is a private, Catholic college providing students with the premier \nstudent-centered experience in Western New York. Students learn and grow with a culturally \ndiverse population that lives its ideals of truth, charity, and unity.  \nMission Statement:  \u201cVilla Maria College, founded by the Felician Sisters, provides students a \nrigorous and enriching educational experience. Offering academic programs with a broad core \ncurriculum, the College transforms and empowers students to realize their intellectual, creative, \nprofessional, and spiritual potential. Inspired by a welcoming Catholic tradition and a dynamic \nFranciscan spirit, Villa Maria College offers individual attention and fosters compassion, justice, \npeace, respect for human dignity and a commitment to service.\u201d \nVilla Maria College Core Values:  \u201cRespect for Human Dignity, Compassion, Transformation, \nSolidarity with the Poor, and Justice & Peace.\u201d \nPOSITION SUMMARY:   \nUnder the daily direction of the Student Success Center staff, the Peer Tutor will, provide \nindividual and small group tutoring to students in the Student Success Center for the College. \nAssist students in improving academic achievement by meeting with them on a regular basis to \nclarify learning problems and work on study skills. Other assistance might include: reviewing \nclass material, discussing the text, helping students with time management, assisting students \nwith the writing process, or working on solutions to problems. \nESSENTIAL RESPONSIBILITIES: \n\uf0b7 Assist students academically in whichever subjects that you have expertise;\n\uf0b7 Develop education resources relevant to your subject area;\n\uf0b7 Facilitate, and track tutorial sessions;\n\uf0b7 Greet and interact with students professionally and enthusiastically;\n\uf0b7 Maintain communications with the Coordinators of the Student Success Center;\n\uf0b7 Encourage students and help them develop academic confidence;\n\uf0b7 Develop study skills specifically designed for the students' needs;\n\uf0b7 Evaluate students' progress in order to see where improvements can be made;\n\uf0b7 Take on additional responsibilities as assigned by the Coordinators of the Student\nSuccess Center;\n\uf0b7 Discuss daily concerns with the Coordinators of the Student Success Center;\n\uf0b7 Support the philosophy and objectives of the College;\n\uf0b7 Other duties as assigned to meet the mission of the College.\n\nQUALIFICATIONS: \n\u2022 Currently enrolled as a student at Villa Maria College;\n\u2022 Cumulative GPA of 3.0 and excelling grades in subjects of expertise;\n\u2022 Microsoft Office (Word, Excel, Power point) knowledge necessary;\n\u2022 Knowledge of industry software to cover disciplines taught at VMC when \napplicable;\n\u2022 Excellent communication and relationship building skills.\nThe above statements are intended to describe the general nature and level of the work being \nperformed by people assigned to this work. This is not an exhaustive list of all duties and \nresponsibilities. Villa Maria College management reserves the right to amend and change \nresponsibilities to meet business and organizational needs as necessary.  \nWORK ENVIRONMENT: \nGeneral classroom environment requires employees to consistently use manual dexterity in \nreaching, writing, navigating around the classroom/office/lab. This work may include hours \nstanding and walking, including up and down stairs, moving items of up to 25-pounds. Evening \nand weekend hours may be needed, on occasion, to perform work associated with this \nposition. \nTo be considered, please complete the online job application at jobs.villa.edu. When you \nhave completed the on-line application process your information will be forwarded to the \nSearch Committee for review. The Search Committee will carefully review each resume and \nthe strongest, most qualified candidates will be contacted for an interview.  \nVilla Maria College is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate on the basis of \nage, race, religion or creed, color, sex, national or ethnic origin, marital status, physical or \nmental disability, or any other protected category by Federal/State guidelines in admissions, \nemployment, or any other aspect regarding the conduct of College programs and activities. \nVILLA MARIA COLLEGE INCLUSION STATEMENT:\nAt Villa Maria College, we value diversity and respect for human dignity as foundations for our\ncollective growth. We develop effective reciprocal relationships based on compassion, trust,\nand authenticity. To fulfill this purpose, we welcome all students and employees who \ncontribute to the richness of our diversity. We work every day to ensure that all who join our \ninclusive community have what they need to realize their full potential."}}, "rows": {"https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Consortium-Student-Wellness-and-Care-Coordinator.pdf": {"school_id": 929, "posting_url": "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/Consortium-Student-Wellness-and-Care-Coordinator.pdf", "job_title_in_post": "Consortium Student Wellness and Care Coordinator", "position_type": "Non-academic", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/VMC-Athletics-Mens-Basketball-Assistant-Coach-PT-Job-Description-002-1.pdf": {"school_id": 929, "posting_url": "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/VMC-Athletics-Mens-Basketball-Assistant-Coach-PT-Job-Description-002-1.pdf", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Coach \u2013 Men\u2019s Basketball", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/VMC-Athletics-Womens-Basketball-Assistant-Coach-PT-Job-Description-003.pdf": {"school_id": 929, "posting_url": "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/VMC-Athletics-Womens-Basketball-Assistant-Coach-PT-Job-Description-003.pdf", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Coach \u2013 Women\u2019s Basketball", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/WFF-Second-Assistant-Coach.pdf": {"school_id": 929, "posting_url": "https://www.villa.edu/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/WFF-Second-Assistant-Coach.pdf", "job_title_in_post": "Second Assistant Coach \u2013 Women\u2019s Flag Football", "position_type": "Unclassified", "job_term": "Part-time", "department_or_school": "", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": ""